{"state": "Nacre School attendance policy, revision 2026-2. A guardian notice excuses an absence if it is operative before the scheduled class start. A guardian may withdraw a notice before that start; a withdrawn notice is then treated as absent. Reinstatement is a new notice and uses its own receipt time. Messages sent after the scheduled start cannot satisfy the advance-notice route, although the separate emergency-review route may be used when an emergency is documented. Office acknowledgements record receipt only and do not prevent withdrawal.\n\nFor Toma's 09:00 class, a guardian submitted \u201cToma will be absent; please excuse\u201d at 07:30. The office acknowledged it at 07:42. At 08:10 the same authenticated guardian wrote, \u201cPlease disregard my excuse; Toma will attend.\u201d Toma did not attend. At 09:20 the guardian wrote, \u201cI should not have withdrawn it; please use the first message.\u201d No emergency or documentation is claimed. The attendance screen still shows the 07:30 message first because it sorts by conversation start.", "model": "ruvector-native-submission-round2-v2", "questions": {"decision": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Is the absence excused under the guardian-notice rule?", "criteria": {"false": "The condition in the question is not established by the operative facts.", "true": "The condition in the question is established by the operative facts."}}}}